{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":44,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T03:08:43.114407Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d325dfa4-ab05-48bb-8f2d-a59128d6f7cf","comment_uuid":"78340b44-4803-4997-ac93-27b96afa97d5","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"Fix committed on fix/34-bootstrap-commit-identity @ 712e1a2b. Root cause was sharper than expected: NOT missing identity but EMPTY-STRING identity - ensure_cache_git_identity guarded on git-config-succeeds, but git config exits 0 for an empty value (this host has empty global user.email/user.name to force per-repo identities), so the empty value skipped the fallback and the commit died with no author; the check also ignored user.name. Fixed: require non-empty user.email AND user.name (git_config_nonempty helper) else fallback. FULL SUITE 2849/0 - first fully-green run of the engagement (the 2 perennial bootstrap failures cleared). sync 58, agent 11, clippy+fmt clean. PR body staged; awaiting operator push.","created_at":"2026-07-29T03:08:43.114294Z","kind":"result"}}
