{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":63,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T06:53:54.198495Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"1a151881-181d-4e06-8c90-e41da1820ad0","title":"Research: is a v3 CI-status writer a known/tracked issue? (design docs, roadmap, dollspace + forecast-bio issue lists)","priority":"low","created_by":"anon-8ea7a055"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":64,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T06:53:59.459621Z","event":{"type":"LabelAdded","issue_uuid":"1a151881-181d-4e06-8c90-e41da1820ad0","label":"research"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":65,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T06:55:59.165256Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1a151881-181d-4e06-8c90-e41da1820ad0","comment_uuid":"5ce598aa-0497-43a3-b33d-ddb3e3e6cdbc","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"Findings: (1) v3 CI-status writer is NOT tracked anywhere except as the split-off half of gh#49 - no dedicated issue on dollspace or forecast-bio, no design/roadmap plan. (2) Root reason: the CI-status 'writer' was NEVER a crosslink command - v2 relied on EXTERNAL CI pipelines dropping meta/ci-status.json into the hub worktree (reader.rs:70, alerts.rs:172; crosslink only reads it). v3 has no worktree, so a v3 path needs a NEW ingestion mechanism (a command/event + a ref home) - undesigned surface, not a port. (3) DESIGN-CROSSLINK-DASHBOARD.md predates v3: ci_failure alert keyed on 'crosslink/hub' (v2); notably it specs unreachable_project as 'git fetch failing for > K cycles' - corroborating that gh#48's fetch-failure-threshold follow-up is the DESIGNED behavior (my impl is a correct subset). (4) OLD-HOME FIND (operator hint): forecast-bio/crosslink#654 - 'dashboard serve crashes silently when serving static assets (v0.9.0-beta.1)' - OPEN, NOT migrated to dollspace. Live high-impact bug: the browser dashboard UI may be unusable on current beta, blocking the whole dashboard surface we've been hardening. Higher priority than the CI-status writer.","created_at":"2026-07-29T06:55:59.165240Z","kind":"result"}}
