{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":89,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T20:12:13.234590Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"fc4f4a98-e11c-4bc9-b415-afb26dc8add9","comment_uuid":"08cdbb68-5f20-4fdc-9e94-5d3815003099","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"Epic read (magnificentlycursed/crosslink#2, the vsdd kickoff bundle): 8 upstream issues dollspace #55-#62 across runtime blocker (#55 stall), flow-integrity (#56 /design --continue resets pipeline.json, #57 swarm phasing doc/code mismatch), enforcement gaps (#58 hook looser than docs, #59 kickoff --container omits no-prompt flag, #60 TIMEOUT sentinel never written), capabilities (#61 effort dial, #62 prompt-injection seam). RE-AUDIT vs develop 6b4f736f: (1) #31 (a #55 contributor) IS fixed on develop [our PR#32]. (2) kickoff_template (#62 partial via PR#44) is on MAIN 26ee1885 only, NOT develop - so #62 seam work is gated on main->develop sync. (3) #59 real: kickoff launch.rs builds permission_flag (skip_permissions/permission_mode, lines 193-197) but need to confirm the ContainerMode branch (229+) applies it to the container's claude invocation - that's the defect. Concrete takeable-now fixes: #56/#57/#58/#59/#60. #55 = investigation (may resolve via #59+#9+#31). #61/#62 = design/gated. Recommend epic's own triage: #59 first (cheap #55 cause), then the defect cluster.","created_at":"2026-08-01T20:12:13.234572Z","kind":"plan"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":90,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T20:15:07.606517Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"fc4f4a98-e11c-4bc9-b415-afb26dc8add9","comment_uuid":"9c3e131d-b757-49dc-b699-6e351e98d1ec","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"#59 ROOT-CAUSED and links to #55. run.rs local branch (:203) passes opts.skip_permissions/permission_mode to launch_local -> build_agent_launch_command emits 'claude{skip_flag}'. Container branch (:241) calls launch_container(mode,worktree,root,image,agent_id,model,allowed_tools,timeout,protected_doc) - does NOT pass the permission flags, and launch_container (launch.rs:666) neither takes nor emits them. Meanwhile container.rs:454 (standalone 'container start') DOES hardcode --dangerously-skip-permissions. => kickoff run --container launches claude with NO permission flag -> claude prompts every tool -> headless container (no TTY) blocks forever = the #55 stall signature exactly. FIX (fix/59-kickoff-container-no-prompt): thread skip_permissions/permission_mode into launch_container and emit the flag on the container's claude invocation, matching launch_local + container start. This is a strong #55 candidate cause for the container path (with #31 already fixed on develop and #9 C-toolchain the other tracked contributor).","created_at":"2026-08-01T20:15:07.606491Z","kind":"observation"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":91,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T20:32:43.878642Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"fc4f4a98-e11c-4bc9-b415-afb26dc8add9","comment_uuid":"50555870-2c8b-4da8-aac8-9bf8f63cc8fa","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"#59 FIXED: commit f1c98a6d on fix/59-kickoff-container-no-prompt. Extracted shared permission_flag() helper; launch_container now takes + emits skip_permissions/permission_mode; run.rs container call site passes opts. Local path unchanged (same helper, existing 14 build_agent_command tests green). New test_permission_flag_postures. clippy+fmt clean. PR body staged (Fixes #59; likely fixes container-path half of #55). Full suite running, then push gate. EPIC PROGRESS: #59 done (this). Next per triage: #55 has 2 known contributors resolved on develop now (#31 hook, #59 container perms) + #9 (C-toolchain, dollspace's container-image issue) - #55 container-path stall should be substantially addressed once #59 merges. Remaining takeable defects: #56 (/design pipeline reset), #57 (swarm phasing doc/code), #58 (hook enforcement), #60 (TIMEOUT sentinel). #61/#62 capabilities (#62 gated on kickoff_template->develop).","created_at":"2026-08-01T20:32:43.878621Z","kind":"result"}}
