{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":105,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T23:24:55.468390Z","event":{"type":"LabelAdded","issue_uuid":"0b04abb9-abe6-452b-ba52-f6ad1e54494e","label":"testing"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":106,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T23:25:47.586635Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0b04abb9-abe6-452b-ba52-f6ad1e54494e","comment_uuid":"48642689-f54d-4598-82ac-4f0be455266c","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"Feasibility confirmed + NEW FINDING. (1) docker 29.6.1 present. (2) Auth: no CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN in env, no ~/.claude/.credentials.json (Keychain host) - live-fire needs the operator to provide a token (best path: ~/.claude/kickoff.env, the designed macOS route). (3) RESIDUAL #55 CAUSE FOUND: kickoff PLAN hardcodes skip_permissions=false + permission_mode=None (plan.rs:248-250) - a plan agent's claude gets NO permission flag in tmux. --allowedTools pre-approves listed tools, but the fresh-worktree TRUST dialog is not covered by allowedTools; run-mode even prints 'Approve trust: tmux attach' expecting a human. Headless plan dispatch = agent parked on the trust prompt = EXACTLY vsdd's #55 signature (plan agents, tmux, never progresses). #59 fixed the container flag; the tmux-plan trust dialog is the likely remaining stall. Retest design: (a) control - global unfixed binary, plan + container kickoffs on a sandbox repo, expect stall; (b) fixed binary from fix/59 worktree + locally-built image, same kickoffs, observe .kickoff-status transitions + docker/tmux logs; (c) pinpoint trust-dialog behavior for the upstream #55 comment.","created_at":"2026-08-01T23:25:47.586618Z","kind":"observation"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":107,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T23:31:39.327923Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0b04abb9-abe6-452b-ba52-f6ad1e54494e","comment_uuid":"ae0d4ccf-b8ce-435c-8819-91c2643175ca","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"PR#65 CI failure triaged + fixed: tests/cli_integration.rs::test_kickoff_dry_run_creates_kickoff_md pinned the PRE-gh#19 behavior (asserted dry-run CREATES worktree+KICKOFF.md - the exact side effect gh#19 removes). Local gate missed it because it ran cargo test --bin only; tests/ is a separate CI step. Fixed b3052d7b: renamed to test_kickoff_dry_run_is_side_effect_free_and_prints_prompt, asserts worktree NOT created + same prompt-contract markers vs stdout. All 6 dry-run integration tests green, fmt clean. Corrected FULL gate (cargo test, all targets) running in background. Memory rule ci-lint-parity updated: gate = clippy + fmt + FULL cargo test, and grep tests/ for old-behavior pins on any behavior change. Awaiting gate -> operator push -> CI rerun. #55 retest plan on hold meanwhile (token prerequisite unchanged).","created_at":"2026-08-01T23:31:39.327901Z","kind":"result"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":108,"timestamp":"2026-08-02T00:04:39.904535Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0b04abb9-abe6-452b-ba52-f6ad1e54494e","comment_uuid":"b5b2b45d-3873-4095-8e94-043f576e058b","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"PR#65 CI GREEN after b3052d7b: Test macos+ubuntu pass, Lint pass, Security Audit pass. All three epic PRs (#63/#64/#65) now open and fully green awaiting dollspace review. Next: #55 live-fire retest, waiting on operator token file.","created_at":"2026-08-02T00:04:39.904521Z","kind":"result"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":109,"timestamp":"2026-08-02T00:09:35.601814Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"0b04abb9-abe6-452b-ba52-f6ad1e54494e","comment_uuid":"41793412-9d6c-445f-8ef7-314806ebb37f","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"#55 RETEST RESULT (control, unfixed binary, tmux plan path): STALL REPRODUCED. tmux pane parked on Claude Code's WORKSPACE-TRUST dialog ('Is this a project you trust? 1. Yes 2. No'), pre-execution - sentinel never progressed, no .kickoff-plan.json. A headless dispatcher (vsdd) never sends the keystroke -> infinite stall = the literal #55 report ('kickoff PLAN agents launch but stall'). MECHANISM CONFIRMED via 'claude --help': 'The workspace trust dialog is skipped when Claude is run in --dangerously-skip-permissions'. Therefore: container path (#59 adds --dangerously-skip-permissions) => trust dialog skipped => container stall FIXED by #59 (proven by mechanism, no image build needed). BUT plan-mode tmux path hardcodes skip_permissions=false/permission_mode=None (plan.rs:248-250) => NO flag => trust dialog => STALL, and NO current PR touches it. CONCLUSION: #59/#9/#10 fix the container contributor but do NOT fix #55-as-filed (plan agents in tmux). The plan-mode trust dialog is a distinct, still-open root cause needing its own fix (design: skip-perms for read-only plan, OR pre-seed folder trust, OR a trust-only bypass).","created_at":"2026-08-02T00:09:35.601797Z","kind":"result"}}
