{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":112,"timestamp":"2026-08-02T00:24:21.303296Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2038d7ff-f85a-451b-9ba8-a65a52b925a5","title":"Deep scan: crosslink best practices + design patterns -> knowledge pages; includes precedent check for user-global config writes (gh#66 fix decision)","priority":"medium","created_by":"anon-8ea7a055"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":113,"timestamp":"2026-08-02T00:24:26.386646Z","event":{"type":"LabelAdded","issue_uuid":"2038d7ff-f85a-451b-9ba8-a65a52b925a5","label":"research"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":114,"timestamp":"2026-08-02T00:31:45.029114Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"2038d7ff-f85a-451b-9ba8-a65a52b925a5","comment_uuid":"c06eeb6f-9807-479d-aebb-f954258df68c","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"Config-conventions scan complete + registered as knowledge page 'config-filesystem-conventions' (tag contributor-reference). DECISION-CRITICAL VERDICT for gh#66: crosslink has ZERO precedent for writing ~/.claude.json or anything under ~/.claude - those are strictly READ-ONLY inputs (container mounts credentials :ro at container.rs:325-334; no .claude.json reference exists in src/ at all). /Users/claire.celesterra writes exist only for crosslink's OWN ~/.crosslink/ state + opt-in shell rc. Option 1 (pre-seed trust into ~/.claude.json) would be a convention-breaking first: writing ANOTHER tool's user-global config. The convention-consistent fix for gh#66 is instead: give kickoff plan the same --skip-permissions/--permission-mode flags kickoff run already has (currently hardcoded false/None at plan.rs:248-250) - matches existing CLI surface, keeps fail-closed default (interactive users keep the trust dialog), lets headless dispatchers (vsdd) pass the flag that documentedly skips the trust dialog. Recommending pivot from option 1 to this. Architecture scan still running.","created_at":"2026-08-02T00:31:45.029096Z","kind":"decision"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":115,"timestamp":"2026-08-02T00:33:20.269459Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"2038d7ff-f85a-451b-9ba8-a65a52b925a5","comment_uuid":"97b83179-959b-4038-b356-7779af338b3d","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"Architecture scan complete + registered as knowledge page 'architecture-code-patterns' (tag contributor-reference). Both pages synced to crosslink/knowledge branch. Key load-bearing patterns: git refs = source of truth / SQLite = derived cache (mutations via SharedWriter events, never direct SQLite on shared path); anyhow bail/context doctrine with INTENTIONAL-comment best-effort writes for monitoring only; argv-vector shell safety with shell_escape_arg for the one true shell string; hermetic test harnesses (run_crosslink, SmokeHarness with bare-remote fork_agent). Scan DONE.","created_at":"2026-08-02T00:33:20.269441Z","kind":"result"}}
