{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":137,"timestamp":"2026-08-02T03:21:22.114244Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"f0a5586e-f6bd-4ba7-8a64-6001f069d77b","comment_uuid":"ec96fe04-4aef-45e1-aaef-88ef65ca061f","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"Design doc complete: .design/dispatch-dials-and-injection-seam.md (knowledge page dispatch-dials-and-injection-seam, tag design-doc, synced). Covers upstream gh#61 (effort/budget dials) + gh#62 (interpolation seam) as one cycle, 2 slices. Interview grounded 4 decisive findings: claude CLI HAS --effort <low|medium|high|xhigh|max> AND --max-budget-usd (so #61 = flags beside --model, no env hack); kickoff_template seam is MAIN-ONLY (26ee1885) not on develop (gates Slice 2); swarm lifecycle.rs:734 hardcodes model:opus; KickoffMetadata types.rs:57 is the R5 recording target. Decisions: D1 budget=per-agent cap; D2 extended placeholder set (+model/effort/doc_path/allowed_tools for R4/R5 manifest echo); D3 Slice 1 (dials, REQ-1-4) lands on develop NOW, Slice 2 (seam, REQ-5-7) held for main->develop sync. 8 REQ / 9 AC / 0 open. Exec-hook (vsdd end-state) = Out of Scope follow-on after per-phase templates. Next: kickoff plan .design/dispatch-dials-and-injection-seam.md to gap-check, then implement Slice 1.","created_at":"2026-08-02T03:21:22.114226Z","kind":"plan"}}
