{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":144,"timestamp":"2026-08-02T03:38:27.008761Z","event":{"type":"LabelAdded","issue_uuid":"1a43ad1e-63e4-411d-9dd9-d09962e545c0","label":"testing"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":145,"timestamp":"2026-08-02T03:41:46.448219Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1a43ad1e-63e4-411d-9dd9-d09962e545c0","comment_uuid":"e87e64a5-762d-4c49-96f1-e12b190cab87","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"#55 RETEST VERDICT: HALF-FIXED. PR#72 (gh#66) clears Dialog 1 (workspace-trust/bypass-perms accept) but NOT Dialog 2 - the settings-pre-approval project-trust prompt ('This folder pre-approves N tool permissions in .claude/settings.json ... trust this folder'). MECHANISM: crosslink init writes allowedTools into .claude/settings.json (merge.rs:217); the tracked file rides into every fresh kickoff worktree; claude's settings-trust gate (v2.1.196+) fires on the untrusted worktree path; --skip-permissions does NOT clear it. Re-raises every launch = structural park. This FALSIFIES PR#72's premise for any crosslink-init'd repo (they all ship tracked tool pre-approvals). INVESTIGATED: no CLI flag/mode clears Dialog 2 ('--settings without trust prompt' = doctor-only; --dangerously-skip-permissions = Dialog 1 + perm checks only). FIX OPTIONS: (A) headless trust pre-grant ~/.claude.json hasTrustDialogAccepted per worktree - the ORIGINALLY-REJECTED #66 approach, now arguably NECESSARY since flags provably don't cover Dialog 2; clears both dialogs; convention cost = crosslink writing ~/.claude (no precedent). (B) strip allowedTools/permissions from the minted worktree's settings.json (keep hooks); agent still gets tools via CLI --allowedTools (launch.rs:226); no ~/.claude write but per-worktree mutation of a tracked file + settings.local.json is ALSO trust-gated (v2.1.207). (C) repo-keyed trust = claude-side, not ours. The retest VINDICATES the original folder-trust pre-grant idea. Design call (revisits convention + is dollspace's kickoff): recommend surfacing to operator+dollspace before implementing.","created_at":"2026-08-02T03:41:46.448205Z","kind":"observation"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":146,"timestamp":"2026-08-02T03:53:42.452526Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1a43ad1e-63e4-411d-9dd9-d09962e545c0","comment_uuid":"cd1a66ee-66eb-48b5-8b79-1d68176bf13d","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"#55 EMPIRICAL INVESTIGATION (host claude 2.1.212). (1) OPTION B REFUTED: trust dialog fires for an EMPTY dir with NO settings.json - stripping tool pre-approvals cannot fix it. (2) OPTION A CONFIRMED: accepting folder-trust wrote projects[path].hasTrustDialogAccepted=true; re-run in the trusted path cleared that dialog - pre-grant is the working mechanism. (3) MULTI-LAYERED: after folder-trust clears, --dangerously-skip-permissions triggers a SEPARATE 'Bypass Permissions mode... Yes I accept' gate. So Option A clears folder-trust but a bypass-mode gate remains. (4) DIVERGENCE: on my host --dangerously-skip-permissions does NOT skip folder-trust (contradicts the downstream retest) - local trust behavior differs from downstream, so the gate sequence must be re-verified downstream before finalizing. CONCLUSION: Option A (pre-grant) necessary+confirmed but likely INSUFFICIENT alone; complete fix = pre-grant + bypass-mode pre-acceptance, verified downstream. NOTE: sandbox trust entries (trust-token/trust-test/trust-empty) were written to ~/.claude.json by the test's accept-dialog step; cleanup blocked by classifier - operator to remove or approve.","created_at":"2026-08-02T03:53:42.452507Z","kind":"observation"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-8ea7a055","agent_seq":147,"timestamp":"2026-08-02T03:57:16.821422Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1a43ad1e-63e4-411d-9dd9-d09962e545c0","comment_uuid":"e109c140-7c7c-4f57-b3e1-aea55fd3aca1","author":"anon-8ea7a055","content":"CLAUDE VERSION CHECK for #55: installed 2.1.212, latest 2.1.220. Read full 2.1.213-220 changelog. LATEST DOES NOT FIX #55 - trend is STRICTER trust: (1) 2.1.218 'hooks now require the agent file's own folder to have accepted workspace trust' -> on >=2.1.218 crosslink's own hooks are ALSO gated on worktree trust = an ADDITIONAL gate. (2) 2.1.218 non-interactive managed-settings consent no longer auto-recorded (stricter). (3) 2.1.218 'trust dialogs name the repository root the grant covers' = cosmetic here: a git worktree is its own repo root (rev-parse --show-toplevel returns the worktree), so each kickoff worktree is still a fresh untrusted root -> still prompts. (4) 2.1.219 adds SDK register_repo_root control request (programmatic repo-root registration) but SDK-ONLY; kickoff uses the CLI in tmux/container -> unavailable. No headless trust-grant flag added; nothing makes --dangerously-skip-permissions skip folder-trust. CONCLUSION: upgrading is not a fix; reinforces Option A (headless folder-trust pre-grant) as necessary + adds a hook-trust gate. DEEPER: this is a Claude Code limitation - the SDK path has register_repo_root, the CLI path has no headless trust grant. RECOMMEND an upstream feature request to Anthropic (a --trust-folder / headless trust-grant flag, or CLI-reachable register_repo_root) since every headless-dispatch tool hits this.","created_at":"2026-08-02T03:57:16.821398Z","kind":"observation"}}
